{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue","id":39107,"title":"Should taint be a bigger issue?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-29T21:26:46-08:00","id":39107,"title":"Should taint be a bigger issue?","content":"In the storyline of aberrant, a great many novas eventually go insane/become deformed by taint. This is in part due to the existence and nature of taint being suppressed by Utopia.<br /> <br /> Players, of course, won't suffer from this lack of knowledge when making and playing a character. Going by what I remember of the old system, a character without any starting taint who is careful with the use of his powers might not get a single dot of permanent taint until Quantum 6 or 7? At that point, you automatically get taint when raising that stat, but even then, it's possible to reach Quantum 10 and have only glowing eyes or a fancy special effects display when you use your powers.<br /> <br /> Will/should the new edition address this? Make taint a more serious problem for players?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:30:09-08:00","id":39109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue#post39107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a character [...] who is careful with the use of his powers might not get a single dot of permanent taint until Quantum 6 or 7</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. Taint is a cheap, easy way to power. You <i>should</i> be able to avoid it if you're responsible and take the hard road to power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T23:12:27-08:00","id":39183,"title":"","content":"I hope not.<br /> <br /> IMO, Taint was a typical White Wolf need to punish characters for wanting to be powerful. All the WoD games needed an angst mechanism and Aberrant was no different.<br /> <br /> That said, it has its place in the setting. It's a quick(er) path to power for characters, but there should be a way for players to choose for their characters to avoid it entirely. There should also be a method for characters to have flashy supers-like power displays and weirdness without having to be a Taint-ridden monster as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T05:02:13-08:00","id":39321,"title":"","content":"I've always viewed Taint more as character limitations.<br /> <br /> Stuff like Superman being vulnerable to Kryptonite, red sun radiation etc. Rogue not being able to touch people without absorbing their personalities or powers, Cyclops always on optic blast, Nightcrawler's inhuman appearance, Hulk having Rage and MPD issues. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> I generally always encouraged my players to take a few points of taint at the start to round out their characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:32:35-08:00","id":39499,"title":"","content":"I for one hope Taint is made much harder to avoid. I've always found Taint comically easy to avoid, and when I run Aberrant I hack the rules to make it much more common. The setting info makes taint out to be a big deal, but the rules just don't bare that out. I've never been a huge fan of the extreme power level of Aberrant, but if Taint is actually an unavoidable side effect of developing great power then I think the setting becomes much more fun and interesting.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T12:48:57-08:00","id":39539,"title":"","content":"I have always seen Taint as the fact that the human body can only hold and use so much power without recoiling and reacting to it. As a result of that, Taint should be easy to get and hard to avoid. Again, I agree that Taint -can- be avoided but you have to work at it very hard. I know several players who try to keep things down since they do not want to be mutated. However, I also know others who go balls to the wall on Taint and buy everything Tainted so that they can get the edge in power early on. So I am in the middle of the spectrum. If I make Taint easier to get, then the guys who do not want to be mutated and are actively working and taking steps to do so get their dreams crushed badly and see all their effort for naught. Although, if I make it harder, then the minmaxers may be at a severe disadvantage. Hmmmm....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T14:08:27-08:00","id":39576,"title":"","content":"Eh. Taint isn\u2019t a \u201cpunishment\u201d, per se; it\u2019s a thematic element of the setting with a massive implication for the overall timeline. At its core, Taint is this: superhuman powers have a dehumanizing influence. <br /> <br /> Looking at the source material for Aberrant, a surprising number of superheroes have decidedly inhuman characteristics \u2014 usually physical, like rocky skin or a pair of bird-like wings sprouting out of one\u2019s shoulder blades; but sometimes psychological. And yes, there\u2019s also the tendency of writers to saddle characters that have great powers with unusual weaknesses as well, such as Superman\u2019s infamous vulnerability to Kryptonite. Taint serves to provide these elements of the superhuman comics; but it does so in a way designed to move the Aberrant era toward the \u00c6on era, when superhumans have become monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T04:53:32-08:00","id":39909,"title":"","content":"Taint really should be fairly easy to avoid if care is taken to do it; it is a symptom of power abuse as much as anything else. Characters who deliberately run their powers too hot too often should get burned with mutations and defects that others avoid, it fits the traditional part of the superhero genre where the heroes look heroic and the villains very often look like weird exaggerations or worse. Evil, greed, and unbridled hubris shows in the comics, and the taint mechanic is how Aberrant goes about simulating it. <br /> <br /> Often characters in comics start out with some unusual features from having extra powerful powers awaken in their origin but then do not change further, the taint option in character generation fits that type well as long as the person does not build up too much taint during play which would be impossible if rising taint levels were inevitable. On the other hand the heroes who are so driven, unscrupulous, or otherwise so obsessed with power or revenge that they are little different from the villains they fight eventually get as twisted as them which also fits the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:07:27-08:00","id":40093,"title":"","content":"My thoughts are threefold:<br /> <br /> 1) Taint should not be harder to avoid.<br /> 2) Taint should provide larger benefits in many cases, so that multiple sources of it are equally valid.<br /> 3) Taint's negative effects should scale up so that you can't go as long without it affecting you at all. A minor drawback of some kind at Taint 2 would be nice.<br /> <br /> The key is that Taint is what creates Supervillains. The Bad Guy is often stronger and tougher than the heroes, because he's one guy and there's four of them, but he's also kind of unstable in ways that don't really map to real-world mental illnesses, and he can't be talked down. That's what Taint does, mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:35:32-08:00","id":40256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue?p=39576#post39576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Taint isn\u2019t a \u201cpunishment\u201d, per se; it\u2019s a thematic element of the setting with a massive implication for the overall timeline. At its core, Taint is this: superhuman powers have a dehumanizing influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The opposite is possible true though right? Maybe not mechanically stated, I think there are powers that can have a very humanizing effect on people.<br /> <br /> This might be because It was one of my favorite parts about All Star Superman. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-o-Imzubmqkc/Tbp9tWqDS4I/AAAAAAAAAA8/uy-_Z65FWnc/s1600/Lex+Luthor+All-Star+Superman.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T10:47:54-08:00","id":40578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue?p=40256#post40256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The opposite is possible true though right? Maybe not mechanically stated, I think there are powers that can have a very humanizing effect on people.<br /> <br /> This might be because It was one of my favorite parts about All Star Superman. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-o-Imzubmqkc/Tbp9tWqDS4I/AAAAAAAAAA8/uy-_Z65FWnc/s1600/Lex+Luthor+All-Star+Superman.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, there are villains who come back from the brink and actually become heroes for a while, or even permanently in rare cases. Lex Luthor has done it both ways in various continuums (on a few occasions even fighting another version of himself), and Magneto flits around the edge between the two with sometimes long forays into either side (though some of his worst acts have been mostly ascribed to an android duplicate) just to name two of the big names who are known for that kind of thing. A way of buying down or otherwise managing taint over time is necessary for simulating characters like that; pinching off the taint outlet in the system would really only choke some story possibilities and not aid the progression to the Aeon setting in any significant way.<br /> <br /> Though leaving the possibility of characters purging taint and coming back to &quot;normal&quot; Nova levels kind of looks like it goes against the fall that ushers in Aeon on the surface it really does not since most of the &quot;monster candidate&quot; villains in the game seem to be addicted to the rush of really pushing their powers and only some very profound slap in the metaphorical face would snap them out of it long enough to reevaluate themselves and make the effort to throw off the taint. The &quot;political&quot; villains who are simply heroes for &quot;the other side&quot; and not on the monster train were just as responsible for the war as the rush monsters though the taint heavy ones ones seem to be the ones who actually &quot;pulled the trigger&quot; and pushed it out of settling into a kind of police vs.criminal cold war into an all out shooting war. You do not need that many monsters to act as that trigger when the rest of the Novas (and the authorities) are wound up tight and staring each other down over the very public atrocities the monsters commit on top of the normal political, religious, and Nova fan &quot;team rivalry&quot; tensions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T14:24:23-08:00","id":40731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue?p=40256#post40256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The opposite is possible true though right? Maybe not mechanically stated, I think there are powers that can have a very humanizing effect on people.<br /> <br /> This might be because It was one of my favorite parts about All Star Superman. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-o-Imzubmqkc/Tbp9tWqDS4I/AAAAAAAAAA8/uy-_Z65FWnc/s1600/Lex+Luthor+All-Star+Superman.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>True; but that\u2019s very definitely the exception to the rule, and isn\u2019t the sort of thing that goes well with game mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T15:18:47-08:00","id":40755,"title":"","content":"When I play Aberrant, I'm not looking for a general comic book simulator. There are dozens of supers games that can simulate the comics. I play Aberrant because of its unique world, and its place within the greater Trinity Continuum. Both the Aberrant setting, and the overarching Continuum setting tells me that the supers of Aberrant are beings of Earth shattering power, but those same beings must struggle against being consumed by the very power that makes them so impressive. That's drama, that's interesting character choices, and that's what makes Aberrant special and set apart form other supers games. It isn't just a comic book simulator. So, while I understand why a less Taint intensive system would make it easier to emulate this comic character or that comic character, that argument does little to move me. I don't want to dilute what makes the Trinity Continuum my favorite game line in the name of generalizeability. I wouldn't be opposed to alternate low taint rules, but I want the base system to be the world described to me in the setting materials, and in that world taint is an ever present threat.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T20:19:15-08:00","id":40898,"title":"","content":"I am not saying taint should not be an ever present threat, what I was getting at was that there is no reason to take it beyond what was in the first edition and turn it into some inevitable 'all Novas must eventually become monsters' thing either. For one thing that kind of inexorable degradation does not fit what is seen in the Aeon Trinity era; despite the popular belief of the neutrals not all Novas became monsters, there are still plenty of sane, relatively normal looking Novas out there in space and some of them are even from as far back as the original crop of Novas. In fact most of the Aberrant monsters seen are the spawn of The Colony and a few other taint-ridden nutcases that keep making trouble and therefore stay in the public eye.<br /> <br /> Also, an ironic effect of the exile of the Novas is that new Nova potentials do not have much in the way of &quot;clean&quot; quantum to trigger eruption, chances are far higher that they will be exposed to taint left from Aberrant incursions and their eruption twisted as a result of being triggered by the taint instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T13:51:21-08:00","id":45108,"title":"","content":"I feel it was just about right last time, and I have high hopes it will be equally cool this time around. If remaining human is important to you, you can keep your humanity. If you hate humanity, you can drown your own humanity out in quantum and taint.<br /> <br /> It felt very Jedi/Sith to me, and it leads to a situation where you chose how to evolve your character and navigate the trade-offs in a meta-game rather than two or three bad die rolls and your character is a ravening, taint-ridden, gibbering beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T03:02:34-08:00","id":45468,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd like to see there being more circumstances where you can usefully gain Taint as a PC, to make it more of a left-hand-path temptation option. As it is, you tend to only get it if you choose to buy stuff tainted. Getting temporary taint is actually pretty hard to do.<br /> <br /> My houserule was to let people take temporary taint for extra successes on a 1-for-1 basis for power rolls, up to maximum of their level in the power. This also helped out with encouraging people to invest in actual levels in the power rather than just maxing out Mega-Attributes after getting a dot in certain powers. I think we also allowed for more frequent fast quantum regain rolls, but with a steadily increasing temporary taint cost the more times you did it within the base interval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/630-vidiian","name":"Vidiian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T11:27:39-08:00","id":66603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue#post39107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Will/should the new edition address this? Make taint a more serious problem for players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would say no. Becoming a mutated and/or insane freak should be an option for players, (and a plot device for NPCs) should they want it, but they shouldn't have it forced on them. I would say the same about limit in Exalted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T05:55:59-08:00","id":67131,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ersatz, you shouldn't punish the player for playing the game. Yes, having a mechanic that says bad things happen if you do X is a staple of White Wolf games and should not go away. However, increasing the difficulty in managing that is something I've seen that turn people away from games or quit tables (at least in other games, I've not had the chance to run or play Aberrant yet). So, no, you don't want to make it a harder issue to deal with in terms of mechanics within the game book. If you want to do it at your table and your players are fine with it, great, but inflicting it on tables that don't want it will probably hurt the game line in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":1575,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","user":"Dairugger","date":". 02-07-2014, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T14:05:24-08:00","id":70030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue?p=45108#post45108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it was just about right last time, and I have high hopes it will be equally cool this time around. If remaining human is important to you, you can keep your humanity. If you hate humanity, you can drown your own humanity out in quantum and taint.<br /> <br /> It felt very Jedi/Sith to me, and it leads to a situation where you chose how to evolve your character and navigate the trade-offs in a meta-game rather than two or three bad die rolls and your character is a ravening, taint-ridden, gibbering beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that you would say that - i once experimented with reworking the Jedi/Sith &quot;dark side of the force&quot; by mining ideas from Taint mechanics for a homebrew game. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T23:17:49-08:00","id":71837,"title":"","content":"I don't believe we need a mechanical representation of taint at all. It always carried the trace of being yet another WW morality cudgel, but it also managed to be entirely superfluous. What is taint really? A manifestation of the corruption humans are afflicted with whenever they have access to power? If that's the case, then it doesn't need any mechanics, it'll happen on its own. As I recall there's a set of optional rules to make the same thing happen to Psions (something about psionic Dysfunctions)? If it's a physical disability from channeling quantum forces, then that indicates that Novas by their very nature should not even exist and are an unstable lifeform, otherwise they would have a natural immunity to the ability their natures give them. An electric eel doesn't electrocute itself after all, why should channeling quantum (the very thing Novas DO) cause them physical harm by itself?<br /> <br /> For those who want to become mutant freaks (like myself) they already put the mechanic in the game as of the player's guide; namely Merits/Flaws.<br /> <br /> If there's a need to track how inhuman a given nova seems to the human world, couldn't we just track their reputation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":". 02-14-2014, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T12:20:38-08:00","id":72135,"title":"","content":"Taint isn't some enforced morality system, or a punishment for players. Taint is an important part of the setting and an inherent part of the game. I have to repeat my earlier argument that Aberrant is not just some supers game. A major part of what makes Aberrant a good game is the setting, and Taint is a major part of that setting. Almost every major organization in the setting takes its stance at least in part based upon its view Taint. Utopia sees it as a major PR problem, Teragen wholeheartedly embraces taint, Proteus sees taint as an indicator of the dangers Novas pose, and Aberrant fears what will Proteus is doing because of its fear of Taint. Taint is a major driving force in the setting an relegating it to the category of a cosmetic choice, or an unnecessary punishment for players strips away what makes Aberrant more interesting than other vanilla supers games.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T13:22:14-08:00","id":72182,"title":"","content":"I wasn't trying to say Taint should go away. I was just trying to say that taint shouldn't be bigger than it is, or by default harder to manage than it is. Yes, taint is a part of the setting and helps set it apart from other supers games. However, it is also part of the setting that taint CAN be managed and I will point to Eden from Aeon as a prime example of that. So yes, it should still be there, it should have deleterious effects and yet have enough of a temptation for players to consider using it. Yet despite all this, it should be manageable.<br /> <br /> If it becomes an unmanageable mess, or at least one too complicated for your average player to potentially do it, then it does become a case of punishing the character. So the developers have to consider the importance and relevancy of taint, and make it a challenge for the players, but a manageable one because if they make it too hard to deal with it will turn away potential players who would otherwise love the game with a more manageable version of taint. I've seen it happen with ST's who were anal retentive on issues of Limit/Resonance/Torment/Paradox in Exalted and people abandon games because of it.<br /> <br /> So as I will continue to say: Yes, taint needs to be in there and probably about as manageable as it was in the existing version of the game otherwise it will cease to be a thing of thematic importance and become the cause of turning Aberrant into just another frustrating game no one but a few die hard fans want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T00:56:15-08:00","id":72509,"title":"","content":"Taint is a setting concept, not just a system one. It's a fact of the setting that novas accumulate taint as they progress in power - this is one of the many reasons that eventually led to the Aberrant war.<br /> <br /> If taint goes (and, knowing the people involved, I feel confident in saying it won't happen), then the game won't be the same - and it'll likely be a game I'm not interested in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T13:10:53-08:00","id":72790,"title":"","content":"In a game now stretching over 10 or more years with a few long brakes in it and my character has managed to get I think a point or two of temporary Taint so it is extremely rare. The only way to really risk Taint, aside for buying Tainted powers, is if you constantly try to overload your power uses and even then it's not a terribly big chance. I didn't even really pay attention to the whole Taint trait there on my char sheet until I joined with the Teragen and started to wonder how on earth will I ever get Chrysalis points at all never mind getting enough to go into an actual Chrysalis. Well perhaps when my year old kid moves out of home my char might have managed to gather a few Chrysalis points, or if looking this positively perhaps even on the verge of his first Chrysalis. Anyway it's unlikely to happen.<br /> <br /> So anyway back to the question at hand. Should Taint be a bigger issue? It depends wholly on what kind of stories you want to tell. Do you want to tell stories of the inevitable slow slide into Taint and the struggle against it by trying to cling to your diminishing humanity? If yes then Taint should be a bigger issue. If you want to tell stories of the Nova Golden Age, then no Taint likely shouldn't be much of an issue. Like said Taint is a setting concept but at the current system it hardly ever comes up unless one deliberately buys Tainted powers.<br /> <br /> So do not loose Taint from the setting but gives us a few optional systems for it, one for low-Taint setting, one for mid-Taint setting and one for high-Taint setting. I know there are some such rulings in the players guide but to my recollection they really aren't that radical to make a huge difference, if I recall correctly they mostly affix permanent Taint costs to buying powers etc. instead of largely affecting gaining temp Taint during game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T09:54:56-08:00","id":74343,"title":"","content":"Not trying to drag this off-topic here...but do you think that there will <i>(or should)</i> be other ways besides joining the Terragen and going thru Chrysalis in order to &quot;shed <b>permanent</b> Taint?&quot; <i>(Really Evolving yourself in the Terragen).</i> I mean, the Terragen is ok...for a bunch of Murdering Psychos <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <i>(Rank and File that is...)</i>, but I'd like to have another way to get rid of permanent Taint, especially without turning into a monster. I don't care if it's &quot;hard &amp; difficult.&quot;<br /> <br /> Back on topic: I think that the original setting had just the right &quot;feel&quot; and the system for how Taint built up in a Nova worked for me -- lessening Taint would weaken it's impact on the world, and increasing Taint would make it overwhelming to the world and characters at large.<br /> <br /> But yeah...I think that Taint should be an integral part of the world. Afterall, the Nova's do eventually become the monstrous Aberrants...and the Psi's need something to &quot;Fight&quot; in the Future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Peace...<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:58:21-08:00","id":74389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue?p=72790#post72790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game now stretching over 10 or more years with a few long brakes in it and my character has managed to get I think a point or two of temporary Taint so it is extremely rare. The only way to really risk Taint, aside for buying Tainted powers, is if you constantly try to overload your power uses and even then it's not a terribly big chance. I didn't even really pay attention to the whole Taint trait there on my char sheet until I joined with the Teragen and started to wonder how on earth will I ever get Chrysalis points at all never mind getting enough to go into an actual Chrysalis. Well perhaps when my year old kid moves out of home my char might have managed to gather a few Chrysalis points, or if looking this positively perhaps even on the verge of his first Chrysalis. Anyway it's unlikely to happen.<br /> <br /> So anyway back to the question at hand. Should Taint be a bigger issue? It depends wholly on what kind of stories you want to tell. Do you want to tell stories of the inevitable slow slide into Taint and the struggle against it by trying to cling to your diminishing humanity? If yes then Taint should be a bigger issue. If you want to tell stories of the Nova Golden Age, then no Taint likely shouldn't be much of an issue. Like said Taint is a setting concept but at the current system it hardly ever comes up unless one deliberately buys Tainted powers.<br /> <br /> So do not loose Taint from the setting but gives us a few optional systems for it, one for low-Taint setting, one for mid-Taint setting and one for high-Taint setting. I know there are some such rulings in the players guide but to my recollection they really aren't that radical to make a huge difference, if I recall correctly they mostly affix permanent Taint costs to buying powers etc. instead of largely affecting gaining temp Taint during game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, an adjustable taint system would probably be best as long as it is not itself too complicated. If the system tries to enforce some kind of Vampire-like inevitable slide or even just causes an excessive amount of bean-counting a lot of groups will simply ignore it altogether or make their own house rules which is its own can of worms. Having an official adjustable system (or even just an official scale for that matter) wold make getting pickup games together or integrating people from different groups smoother since everyone could sync with the setting on the taint dial for that particular game so to speak.<br /> <br /> People invariably want to bring in characters that do not fit well with a narrow, fixed taint formula; they are not usually the majority but there is no reason to summarily exclude them either. In a (more or less) round robin game I ran the characters ranged from one who had a very bad eruption and had to push hard to survive at first and entered the campaign with the realization that she had to go easy and let her significant taint load bleed off or be consumed by it, to one who was a squeaky clean starry-eyed &quot;Feisty Disney Princess&quot; type who did not know what this &quot;dark side&quot; of quantum she heard people talking about was and never built up enough to notice, with the other characters somewhere in the middle. While extreme opposites and skirting the limits of the system both concepts are valid enough on a setting and a game system level in the original game and really should be doable in the new one too. Draconian &quot;thou shalt descend into a tainted monster&quot; (and other similar rules on rails) systems only limit the concepts possible which tends to disappoint players who do not like to march in lockstep so they do not get into the spirit of the story as much as they should and even sometimes drop out of the game altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:56:07-07:00","id":97520,"title":"","content":"My feeling on Taint is that it should be a major part of characters, but that it should also have some mechanical tweaks to make it more than just getting tentacles coming out of your forehead or whatever. Taint should represent your character evolving more toward whatever type of post-human being your powers and personality would send you down. <br /> <br /> Someone posted a scene from All-Star Superman earlier, that shows that the mere fact of Superman's omniscience leads to an enlightened desire to help people. That's an aberration! This is a being who sees the interconnectedness of all things, every moment of his life, to such a degree that he can't help but feel overwhelming empathy for those around him. That's going to remove you from the experience of baseline humanity just as thoroughly as any other aberration. <br /> <br /> My hope for the new Aberrant is that Taint has a much greater mechanical impact, but that it also be used to reinforce your character's move away from humanity in a more interesting way. To my mind, the single greatest example of a high-Taint nova in comics is Dr. Manhattan. He doesn't turn into Cthulhu or start rampaging through New York - he just loses the ability to think like a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:55:08-07:00","id":102184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/39107-should-taint-be-a-bigger-issue?p=97520#post97520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My feeling on Taint is that it should be a major part of characters, but that it should also have some mechanical tweaks to make it more than just getting tentacles coming out of your forehead or whatever. Taint should represent your character evolving more toward whatever type of post-human being your powers and personality would send you down.<br /> <br /> Someone posted a scene from All-Star Superman earlier, that shows that the mere fact of Superman's omniscience leads to an enlightened desire to help people. That's an aberration! This is a being who sees the interconnectedness of all things, every moment of his life, to such a degree that he can't help but feel overwhelming empathy for those around him. That's going to remove you from the experience of baseline humanity just as thoroughly as any other aberration.<br /> <br /> My hope for the new Aberrant is that Taint has a much greater mechanical impact, but that it also be used to reinforce your character's move away from humanity in a more interesting way. To my mind, the single greatest example of a high-Taint nova in comics is Dr. Manhattan. He doesn't turn into Cthulhu or start rampaging through New York - he just loses the ability to think like a human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's kind of my thought on it as well. My longest-run Aberrant character wasn't a Teragen member per se (since that will wreck havoc on US security clearances) but she very much realized that she was no longer human after using a couple months of &quot;needing to hide due to shenanigans&quot; time to teleport herself far enough out into space that she ran into Voyager and was reminded that she had a place to go back to. She came back rather different than the woman she had been when she left and I enjoyed playing that shift in viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}